proofs.description:
The full cross form agrees with the actual row table on pinned inputs.
Orthogonal tests put its channel value in the same-sign protected space;
the first table injection flag forces the pinned vector to zero.

Half of the epsilon budget pays the common-annihilator dimension loss
for every minus rank. The other half pays the fixed 16^c prefactor,
using only that the total nominal rank is at least one.

Cover the large-kernel event by the zero-image events of all bounded
coefficient certificates. Each valid certificate satisfies the cap;
invalid ones contribute an empty event. Apply the finite union bound.

Project a table dependence onto each endpoint. Absorb each point-ray
coefficient into its affine base vector and apply the stronger cover;
the constant coordinate identifies that coefficient.
